{"title":"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/3/5637fc75c9c9da168b51f81b23865cc654f02831.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A(11, 9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f45605e2d1092abdc7f8ff726507a664ca582a97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(2, -3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> are vertices of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/9/3c99bbe74cccdc92b249d376f13d9429d41a8b7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />. The altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> meets the opposite side at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b93a6c5c49cbd77f587aa830e632f576585b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(-1, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. What are the coordinates of point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/4/2b48be0a6bc04615eda7bb3c23b49b8f6fb5a987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ (-8, 9)\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ (-4, 8)\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ (-4, 9)\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ (-2, 3)\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ (-1, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"575\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ac37c9fa391eebb9601bfaca8bfbfaabdf5ca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = AC$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is isosceles, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/383377396cd2b6bd95f64d0e79ecd0f0eac25dad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = CD$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, the coordinates of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/1/a91e096a8783312bc8c982fbc2c68cc751e653ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1 - 3, 3 + 6) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } (-4,9)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"244\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/6/4e64b7d6c733817509b22e4cdd26b7aa91ed42a2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D; A=(11,9); B=(2,-3); C=(-4,9); D=(-1,3); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--D); draw(rightanglemark(A,D,B,30)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Calculating the equation of the line running between points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4dd8e3fd5bd866cf3f796d90e93e68f26e91fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -2x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"15\" />. The only coordinate of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that is also on this line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19cf935578c84bbbc3ee1b03236afae1d921ced5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } (-4,9)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"101\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to the first solution, because the triangle is isosceles, then the line drawn in the middle separates the triangle into two smaller congruent triangles. To get from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, we go to the left <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then to get to point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> from point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, we go to the right <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, getting us the coordinates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19cf935578c84bbbc3ee1b03236afae1d921ced5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } (-4,9)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"101\" height=\"29\" />. ~<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/b/eab10c25a519751033aabcf20d0e967f40c170e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{KLBBC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As stated in solution 1, the triangle is isosceles. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/c/d6c903419860d4d2d6fb832a27d73e8e7acd40ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A,B,C,D; A=(11,9); B=(2,-3); C=(-4,9); D=(-1,3); draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--D); draw(rightanglemark(A,D,B)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,E); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,W); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b93a6c5c49cbd77f587aa830e632f576585b36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D(-1, 3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f45605e2d1092abdc7f8ff726507a664ca582a97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B(2, -3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/9/8b90c2d963ad6794060e1af0ec699535f6f4fb59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c8877d6287b0ffe4decc09444cadf092e85c1891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8e8719e9350ec8fb3f5f78d294fe054a0553bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d924f912a4072521e9bb4c86d868591e01d0f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. Similarly for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90a3eadfea1b6fbed304f9f0f4cb34d158d3f3e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y-3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/e/f8efbb365872f10643bb6056bd2b770e68243805.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=3$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c1b3337268879246336b597a1b8d88b2f17019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. So our final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19cf935578c84bbbc3ee1b03236afae1d921ced5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) } (-4,9)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"101\" height=\"29\" />. \n</p><p>- youtube.com/indianmathguy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/4rRckA3gcPU\">https://youtu.be/4rRckA3gcPU</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/XRfOULUmWbY?t=367\">https://youtu.be/XRfOULUmWbY?t=367</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B\">2017 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017022538\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.041 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.062 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 315/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2320/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 154/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7736/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.183      1 -total\n 60.11%    8.525      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.91%    5.519      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15424:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017022538 and revision id 263821. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}